IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `jp-ai-domain`
IMPORT `jp-ai-articles`

-- Japan: Act No. 53 of 2025 (令和七年法律第五十三号) -- WHAT THE ACT MEANS FOR A
-- BUSINESS OPERATOR.
-- A DRAFT. Not for use as advice. No domain expert and no lawyer qualified in
-- Japan has read this encoding against the source.
--
-- SEAT: a business operator that develops, provides or uses AI-related
-- technology. The provisions that speak to it are Article 2 (the definition that
-- makes it an operator), Article 7 (its two responsibilities), Article 6 (if it
-- is also a research and development institute), Article 16 (what the national
-- government is to do toward it), Article 25 (what the Headquarters may ask of
-- it), and Supplementary Provisions Article 1 (from when). The absence findings
-- -- no reporting duty, no penalty, no naming, no investigation or order power --
-- are computed from the provisions table in jp-ai-articles.l4.
--
-- Every rule below that reads the date takes it as an input: "in force as of
-- date D". The day the Cabinet Order fixed for Chapters III and IV is an input
-- too, because the Cabinet Order is not deposited; it is needed only for a date
-- inside the window Supplementary Provisions Article 1 gives the Order.

§ `When the provisions take effect (Supplementary Provisions Article 1)`

-- src:5 | (Act No. 53 of June 4, 2025)
-- The day of promulgation is the date in the Act's own citation; the e-Gov XML
-- carries it as Era=Reiwa Year=07 PromulgateMonth=06 PromulgateDay=04, and the
-- e-Gov law register gives promulgation_date 2025-06-04 (egov-laws-search.json).
@ref Act No. 53 of June 4, 2025 (src:5)
GIVETH A DATE
`the day of promulgation` MEANS Date 4 6 2025

DECLARE `Commencement` IS ONE OF
    `in force`
    `not yet in force`
    `in force from a day fixed by Cabinet Order, and that day was not given`
    `the Cabinet Order day given is outside the window Supplementary Provisions Article 1 allows`

-- src:347 | Article 1 This Act comes into effect on the date of promulgation; provided,
-- 日本語 (authoritative):
-- src:ai-act-ja:90 | 第一条 この法律は、公布の日から施行する。
@ref Supplementary Provisions Article 1, main clause (src:347) (src:ai-act-ja:90)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Commencement`
`commencement of the main provisions on` d MEANS
    IF   d AT LEAST `the day of promulgation`
    THEN `in force`
    ELSE `not yet in force`

-- src:348 | however, that the provisions of Chapters III and IV, and Article 3 and Article 4
-- src:349 | of the Supplementary Provisions come into effect on the day specified by
-- src:353 | Cabinet Order within a period not exceeding three months from the date of
-- src:354 | promulgation.
-- 日本語 (authoritative):
-- src:ai-act-ja:91 | ただし、第三章及び第四章並びに附則第三条及び第四条の規定は、公布の日から起算して三月を超えない範囲内において政令で定める日から施行する。
-- The Act bounds the day ("within a period not exceeding three months from the
-- date of promulgation") but does not name it. e-Gov's current revision carries
-- the enforcement date 2025-09-01 (egov-law-revisions.json); the Cabinet Order
-- itself is not deposited, so the day is an input, and it is needed only inside
-- the window.
--
-- Read from the text alone, the proviso gives three answers when no day is given:
-- before promulgation, not in force; from promulgation to the end of the window,
-- the Cabinet Order day is needed; from the last day of the window, in force,
-- because no day the Order could fix is later (fork F11). A day that is given is
-- checked against the window first, and a day outside it is flagged rather than
-- used, even on a date before promulgation (assumed, not ruled).
@ref Supplementary Provisions Article 1, proviso (src:348-354) (src:ai-act-ja:91)
GIVEN d IS A DATE, `the day fixed by Cabinet Order` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Commencement`
`commencement of Chapters III and IV on` d `the day fixed by Cabinet Order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day fixed by Cabinet Order`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        BRANCH IF d LESS THAN `the day of promulgation`
               THEN `not yet in force`
               IF d AT LEAST `the last day the Cabinet Order could fix`
               THEN `in force`
               OTHERWISE `in force from a day fixed by Cabinet Order, and that day was not given`
    WHEN JUST o THEN
        BRANCH IF    o LESS THAN `the day of promulgation`
                  OR `the last day the Cabinet Order could fix` LESS THAN o
               THEN `the Cabinet Order day given is outside the window Supplementary Provisions Article 1 allows`
               IF d AT LEAST o
               THEN `in force`
               OTHERWISE `not yet in force`

-- The last day of the proviso's window (quoted above). 公布の日から起算して counts
-- the day of promulgation as day one, so three months run from 2025-06-04 and end
-- on 2025-09-03, the day before the corresponding day of the third month. A reader
-- who leaves the first day out gets 2025-09-04. The later day is taken (fork F11),
-- so that "in force" on or after it holds on either count, and a given day of
-- 2025-09-04 is accepted rather than flagged.
@ref Supplementary Provisions Article 1, proviso, the end of the window
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day the Cabinet Order could fix` MEANS Date 4 9 2025

§ `Who is a utilization business operator (Articles 2 and 7)`

-- src:35 | Article 2 The term "artificial intelligence-related technology" as used in this Act
-- src:36 | means technology necessary for realizing the function to substitute intellectual
-- src:37 | abilities for human cognition, inference and judgement by artificial means, and
-- src:38 | technology relating to information processing systems for realizing the function
-- src:39 | to process the input information and output that result by using the technology.
-- 日本語 (authoritative):
-- src:ai-act-ja:13 | 第二条 この法律において、「人工知能関連技術」とは、人工的な方法により人間の認知、推論及び判断に係る知的な能力を代替する機能を実現するために必要な技術並びに入力された情報を当該技術を利用して処理し、その結果を出力する機能を実現するための情報処理システムに関する技術をいう。
@ref Article 2 (src:35-39) (src:ai-act-ja:13)
GIVEN t IS A `The technology`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 2: AI-related technology` t MEANS
        t's `technology necessary for realizing the function of substituting, by artificial means, intellectual abilities relating to human cognition, inference and judgement`
    OR  t's `technology relating to an information processing system that processes input information using that technology and outputs the result`

-- src:133 | Article 7 Any person who intends to develop or provide products or services that
-- src:134 | utilize artificial intelligence-related technology, or other persons who intend to
-- src:135 | utilize other artificial intelligence-related technology in their business
-- src:136 | activities (referred to below as a "utilization business operator"), is to endeavor
-- 日本語 (authoritative):
-- src:ai-act-ja:30 | 第七条 人工知能関連技術を活用した製品又はサービスの開発又は提供をしようとする者その他の人工知能関連技術を事業活動において活用しようとする者（以下「活用事業者」という。）は、基本理念にのっとり、自ら積極的な人工知能関連技術の活用により事業活動の効率化及び高度化並びに新産業の創出に努めるとともに、第四条の規定に基づき国が実施する施策及び第五条の規定に基づき地方公共団体が実施する施策に協力しなければならない。
-- 活用事業者. その他の joins the two descriptions of persons: the developer or
-- provider is an instance of the wider class of persons who use the technology
-- in business (fork F2). The translation's second "other" ("utilize other
-- artificial intelligence-related technology") has no counterpart in the Japanese.
@ref Article 7, definition of a utilization business operator (src:133-136) (src:ai-act-ja:30)
GIVEN b IS A `The business`, t IS A `The technology`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 7: a utilization business operator` b t MEANS
        (    b's `develops or provides, or intends to develop or provide, products or services that use the technology`
         OR  b's `uses, or intends to use, the technology in its business activities`)
    AND `Article 2: AI-related technology` t

§ `What Article 7 asks of a business operator`

DECLARE `Article 7 endeavor answer` IS ONE OF
    `I am to endeavor to make my business activities more efficient and advanced, and to create new industries, by actively using the technology`
    `Article 7's endeavor does not apply: not a utilization business operator`
    `Article 7's endeavor was not yet in force`

-- src:136 | activities (referred to below as a "utilization business operator"), is to endeavor
-- src:137 | to enhance the efficiency and advancement of business activities and create
-- src:138 | new industries through active utilization of artificial intelligence -related
-- 日本語 (authoritative):
-- src:ai-act-ja:30 | 第七条 人工知能関連技術を活用した製品又はサービスの開発又は提供をしようとする者その他の人工知能関連技術を事業活動において活用しようとする者（以下「活用事業者」という。）は、基本理念にのっとり、自ら積極的な人工知能関連技術の活用により事業活動の効率化及び高度化並びに新産業の創出に努めるとともに、第四条の規定に基づき国が実施する施策及び第五条の規定に基づき地方公共団体が実施する施策に協力しなければならない。
-- 努める: an endeavor. Whether the しなければならない that closes the sentence
-- also governs this limb is fork F1; on either reading no consequence is stated.
@ref Article 7, first limb (src:136-138) (src:ai-act-ja:30)
GIVEN d IS A DATE, b IS A `The business`, t IS A `The technology`
GIVETH AN `Article 7 endeavor answer`
`Article 7: what the business is to endeavor to do` d b t MEANS
    BRANCH IF `commencement of the main provisions on` d EQUALS `not yet in force`
           THEN `Article 7's endeavor was not yet in force`
           IF (NOT (`Article 7: a utilization business operator` b t))
           THEN `Article 7's endeavor does not apply: not a utilization business operator`
           OTHERWISE `I am to endeavor to make my business activities more efficient and advanced, and to create new industries, by actively using the technology`

DECLARE `Article 7 cooperation answer` IS ONE OF
    `I must cooperate with the measure (Article 7, 協力しなければならない), and the Act states no sanction for not cooperating`
    `Article 7 does not reach this measure: it is not implemented by the national government under Article 4 or by a local government under Article 5`
    `Article 7's duty to cooperate does not apply: not a utilization business operator`
    `Article 7's duty to cooperate was not yet in force`

-- src:139 | technology, and must cooperate with the measures implemented by the
-- src:140 | national government under the provisions of Article 4 and by a local
-- src:141 | government under the provisions of Article 5, in accordance with the basic
-- src:142 | principles.
-- 日本語 (authoritative):
-- src:ai-act-ja:30 | 第七条 人工知能関連技術を活用した製品又はサービスの開発又は提供をしようとする者その他の人工知能関連技術を事業活動において活用しようとする者（以下「活用事業者」という。）は、基本理念にのっとり、自ら積極的な人工知能関連技術の活用により事業活動の効率化及び高度化並びに新産業の創出に努めるとともに、第四条の規定に基づき国が実施する施策及び第五条の規定に基づき地方公共団体が実施する施策に協力しなければならない。
-- 協力しなければならない: "must cooperate". The verb is the strongest in the Act
-- addressed to anyone outside government, and it is still a duty with no sanction:
-- the provisions table records no mechanism on any row (jp-ai-articles.l4).
@ref Article 7, second limb (src:139-142) (src:ai-act-ja:30)
GIVEN d IS A DATE, b IS A `The business`, t IS A `The technology`, m IS A `The measure`
GIVETH AN `Article 7 cooperation answer`
`Article 7: must the business cooperate with the measure` d b t m MEANS
    BRANCH IF `commencement of the main provisions on` d EQUALS `not yet in force`
           THEN `Article 7's duty to cooperate was not yet in force`
           IF (NOT (`Article 7: a utilization business operator` b t))
           THEN `Article 7's duty to cooperate does not apply: not a utilization business operator`
           IF     m's `implemented by the national government under Article 4`
               OR m's `implemented by a local government under Article 5`
           THEN `I must cooperate with the measure (Article 7, 協力しなければならない), and the Act states no sanction for not cooperating`
           OTHERWISE `Article 7 does not reach this measure: it is not implemented by the national government under Article 4 or by a local government under Article 5`

§ `What Article 6 asks of a business that is also a research and development institute`

DECLARE `Article 6 answer` IS ONE OF
    `I am to endeavor to research, develop and disseminate, to develop human resources, to endeavor to cooperate with Article 4 and Article 5 measures, and to endeavor to do interdisciplinary research`
    `Article 6 does not apply: not a research and development institute`
    `Article 6 was not yet in force`

-- src:106 | Article 6 (1) A university, a research and development corporation prescribed in
-- src:107 | Article 2, paragraph (9) of the Act for Activation of Science, Technology and
-- src:108 | Innovation Creation (Act No. 63 of 2008), and other institutes that research
-- src:109 | and develop artificial intelligence-related technology (referred to below as a
-- src:110 | "research and development institute") are to endeavor positively to research
-- src:111 | and develop artificial intelligence-related technology, to disseminate their
-- src:112 | results, and to develop human resources that have expert and broad knowledge
-- src:113 | as well as endeavor to cooperate with the measures implemented by the
-- src:114 | national government under the provisions of Article 4 and by a local
-- src:115 | government under the provisions of the preceding Article, in accordance with
-- src:116 | the basic principles.
-- 日本語 (authoritative):
-- src:ai-act-ja:26 | 第六条 大学、科学技術・イノベーション創出の活性化に関する法律（平成二十年法律第六十三号）第二条第九項に規定する研究開発法人その他の人工知能関連技術の研究開発を行う機関（以下「研究開発機関」という。）は、基本理念にのっとり、人工知能関連技術の研究開発及びその成果の普及並びに専門的かつ幅広い知識を有する人材の育成に積極的に努めるとともに、第四条の規定に基づき国が実施する施策及び前条の規定に基づき地方公共団体が実施する施策に協力するよう努めるものとする。
-- src:123 | (3) In promoting effectively research and development of artificial intelligence -
-- src:124 | related technology, a research and development institute is to endeavor to
-- src:125 | conduct interdisciplinary or comprehensive research and development, in light
-- src:126 | of the necessity to comprehensively utilize knowledge in various fields in
-- src:127 | humanities and natural sciences.
-- 日本語 (authoritative):
-- src:ai-act-ja:28 | ３ 研究開発機関は、人工知能関連技術の研究開発を効果的に進めるに当たっては、人文科学及び自然科学に関する多様な分野の知見を総合的に活用することが必要であることに鑑み、学際的又は総合的な研究開発に努めるものとする。
-- Whether a company that researches and develops AI-related technology is one of
-- the "other institutes" (その他の...機関) is fork F6; the business states it.
@ref Article 6(1) and (3) (src:106-116) (src:123-127) (src:ai-act-ja:26) (src:ai-act-ja:28)
GIVEN d IS A DATE, b IS A `The business`, t IS A `The technology`
GIVETH AN `Article 6 answer`
`Article 6: what the business is to endeavor to do as a research and development institute` d b t MEANS
    BRANCH IF `commencement of the main provisions on` d EQUALS `not yet in force`
           THEN `Article 6 was not yet in force`
           IF (NOT (     b's `a university, a research and development corporation, or another institute that researches and develops the technology`
                     AND `Article 2: AI-related technology` t))
           THEN `Article 6 does not apply: not a research and development institute`
           OTHERWISE `I am to endeavor to research, develop and disseminate, to develop human resources, to endeavor to cooperate with Article 4 and Article 5 measures, and to endeavor to do interdisciplinary research`

§ `Article 16: the national government's research, and what it may do toward the business`

-- src:214 | Article 16 The national government is to collect information on trends of
-- src:215 | research and development, and utilization of artificial intelligence-related
-- src:216 | technology both domestically and internationally, analyze cases where the
-- src:217 | citizens' rights and interests are infringed due to research and development, or
-- src:221 | utilization of artificial intelligence-related technology by wrongful purposes or
-- src:222 | inappropriate methods, consider measures based on the analyzation, and
-- 日本語 (authoritative):
-- src:ai-act-ja:49 | 第十六条 国は、国内外の人工知能関連技術の研究開発及び活用の動向に関する情報の収集、不正な目的又は不適切な方法による人工知能関連技術の研究開発又は活用に伴って国民の権利利益の侵害が生じた事案の分析及びそれに基づく対策の検討その他の人工知能関連技術の研究開発及び活用の推進に資する調査及び研究を行い、その結果に基づいて、研究開発機関、活用事業者その他の者に対する指導、助言、情報の提供その他の必要な措置を講ずるものとする。
@ref Article 16, the cases the national government analyzes (src:214-222) (src:ai-act-ja:49)
GIVEN i IS A `The incident`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 16: a case of the kind the national government analyzes` i MEANS
        i's `citizens' rights and interests were infringed`
    AND (   i's `arose from research and development or utilization of the technology for a wrongful purpose`
         OR i's `arose from research and development or utilization of the technology by an inappropriate method`)

DECLARE `Article 16 answer` IS ONE OF
    `the national government is to give me guidance, advice and information, or take other necessary measures, based on its research; the Act states no duty to follow them`
    `Article 16 was not yet in force`

-- src:225 | the national government based on the results, is to give guidance, advice to a
-- src:226 | research and development institute, a utilization business operator and other
-- src:227 | people, and provide information for them, or take other necessary measures.
-- 日本語 (authoritative):
-- src:ai-act-ja:49 | 第十六条 国は、国内外の人工知能関連技術の研究開発及び活用の動向に関する情報の収集、不正な目的又は不適切な方法による人工知能関連技術の研究開発又は活用に伴って国民の権利利益の侵害が生じた事案の分析及びそれに基づく対策の検討その他の人工知能関連技術の研究開発及び活用の推進に資する調査及び研究を行い、その結果に基づいて、研究開発機関、活用事業者その他の者に対する指導、助言、情報の提供その他の必要な措置を講ずるものとする。
-- 研究開発機関、活用事業者その他の者: the class reaches research and development
-- institutes, utilization business operators "and other people", so the answer
-- does not turn on being an operator. "Other necessary measures" (その他の必要な
-- 措置) is not defined; the Act does not say that it includes publishing a name.
@ref Article 16, guidance, advice and information (src:225-227) (src:ai-act-ja:49)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Article 16 answer`
`Article 16: what the national government is to do toward the business` d MEANS
    IF   `commencement of the main provisions on` d EQUALS `not yet in force`
    THEN `Article 16 was not yet in force`
    ELSE `the national government is to give me guidance, advice and information, or take other necessary measures, based on its research; the Act states no duty to follow them`

§ `Article 25: what the Artificial Intelligence Strategic Headquarters may ask`

DECLARE `Article 25 answer` IS ONE OF
    `the Headquarters may ask me for necessary cooperation if it finds it particularly necessary (Article 25(2)); Article 25 states no duty to comply`
    `the Headquarters may ask me for necessary cooperation if it finds it particularly necessary (Article 25(2)); and if the request is an Article 4 measure, Article 7 says I must cooperate`
    `the Headquarters may request materials, opinions, explanations or other cooperation if it finds it necessary (Article 25(1)); Article 25 states no duty to comply`
    `the Headquarters may request materials, opinions, explanations or other cooperation if it finds it necessary (Article 25(1)); and if the request is an Article 4 measure, Article 7 says I must cooperate`
    `Article 25 was not yet in force`
    `Article 25 is in force from a day fixed by Cabinet Order, and that day was not given`
    `whether Article 25 was in force cannot be answered: the Cabinet Order day given is outside the window Supplementary Provisions Article 1 allows`

-- src:314 | Article 25 (1) If the headquarters finds it necessary for performing the affairs
-- src:315 | under their jurisdiction, they may request the heads of a relevant
-- 日本語 (authoritative):
-- src:ai-act-ja:80 | 第二十五条 本部は、その所掌事務を遂行するため必要があると認めるときは、関係行政機関、地方公共団体、独立行政法人（独立行政法人通則法（平成十一年法律第百三号）第二条第一項に規定する独立行政法人をいう。）及び地方独立行政法人（地方独立行政法人法（平成十五年法律第百十八号）第二条第一項に規定する地方独立行政法人をいう。）の長並びに特殊法人（法律により直接に設立された法人又は特別の法律により特別の設立行為をもって設立された法人であって、総務省設置法（平成十一年法律第九十一号）第四条第一項第八号の規定の適用を受けるものをいう。）の代表者に対して、資料の提出、意見の表明、説明その他必要な協力を求めることができる。
-- src:329 | (2) If the headquarters finds it particularly necessary for performing the affairs
-- src:330 | under their jurisdiction, they may ask for necessary cooperation from a person
-- src:331 | other than those prescribed in the preceding paragraph.
-- 日本語 (authoritative):
-- src:ai-act-ja:81 | ２ 本部は、その所掌事務を遂行するために特に必要があると認めるときは、前項に規定する者以外の者に対しても、必要な協力を依頼することができる。
-- 依頼することができる (paragraph 2, "may ask for") is softer than paragraph (1)'s
-- 求めることができる ("may request"); neither paragraph states a duty to comply
-- or a consequence. Whether a request from the Headquarters is a measure "under
-- the provisions of Article 4", so that Article 7 makes cooperation a duty, is
-- fork F5: the business states it, and the answer says which reading it took.
-- Paragraph (1) reaches the representative of a special corporation (特殊法人の
-- 代表者), and a special corporation that uses the technology in its business is a
-- utilization business operator too, so fork F5 is asked in both paragraphs.
@ref Article 25(1) and (2) (src:314-315) (src:329-331) (src:ai-act-ja:80) (src:ai-act-ja:81)
GIVEN d IS A DATE, `the day fixed by Cabinet Order` IS A MAYBE DATE, b IS A `The business`, t IS A `The technology`, m IS A `The measure`
GIVETH AN `Article 25 answer`
`Article 25: what the Headquarters may ask of the business` d `the day fixed by Cabinet Order` b t m MEANS
    CONSIDER `commencement of Chapters III and IV on` d `the day fixed by Cabinet Order`
    WHEN `not yet in force` THEN `Article 25 was not yet in force`
    WHEN `in force from a day fixed by Cabinet Order, and that day was not given` THEN `Article 25 is in force from a day fixed by Cabinet Order, and that day was not given`
    WHEN `the Cabinet Order day given is outside the window Supplementary Provisions Article 1 allows` THEN `whether Article 25 was in force cannot be answered: the Cabinet Order day given is outside the window Supplementary Provisions Article 1 allows`
    WHEN `in force` THEN
        BRANCH IF     b's `the head of a relevant administrative body, local government or incorporated administrative agency, or the representative of a special corporation`
                  AND `Article 7: a utilization business operator` b t
                  AND m's `implemented by the national government under Article 4`
               THEN `the Headquarters may request materials, opinions, explanations or other cooperation if it finds it necessary (Article 25(1)); and if the request is an Article 4 measure, Article 7 says I must cooperate`
               IF b's `the head of a relevant administrative body, local government or incorporated administrative agency, or the representative of a special corporation`
               THEN `the Headquarters may request materials, opinions, explanations or other cooperation if it finds it necessary (Article 25(1)); Article 25 states no duty to comply`
               IF     `Article 7: a utilization business operator` b t
                  AND m's `implemented by the national government under Article 4`
               THEN `the Headquarters may ask me for necessary cooperation if it finds it particularly necessary (Article 25(2)); and if the request is an Article 4 measure, Article 7 says I must cooperate`
               OTHERWISE `the Headquarters may ask me for necessary cooperation if it finds it particularly necessary (Article 25(2)); Article 25 states no duty to comply`

§ `What the Act does not contain, computed from the provisions table`

-- These read the table in jp-ai-articles.l4. Each takes the table as an input so
-- that jp-ai-tests.l4 can show the answer moving when a (synthetic) row carries
-- a mechanism; the baseline passes `the provisions of the Act`.

GIVEN m IS A `Mechanism`, ps IS A LIST OF `A provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`some provision carries` m ps MEANS
    any (GIVEN p YIELD elem m (p's `mechanisms affecting a private person`)) ps

DECLARE `Reporting answer` IS ONE OF
    `no provision of this Act requires me to report it; the national government is to analyze cases like this one (Article 16)`
    `no provision of this Act requires me to report it`
    `a provision of this Act carries a duty to report`
    `this Act was not yet in force`

-- Searched: every row of the table (Articles 1 to 28 and the Supplementary
-- Provisions). The nearest provision is Article 16, under which the NATIONAL
-- GOVERNMENT collects information and analyzes cases; it addresses no duty to the
-- business.
@ref Articles 1 to 28 and Supplementary Provisions Articles 1 to 4, searched for a reporting duty; Article 16
GIVEN d IS A DATE, i IS A `The incident`, ps IS A LIST OF `A provision`
GIVETH A `Reporting answer`
`must the business report the incident` d i ps MEANS
    BRANCH IF `commencement of the main provisions on` d EQUALS `not yet in force`
           THEN `this Act was not yet in force`
           IF `some provision carries` `a duty to report an incident or a case to an authority` ps
           THEN `a provision of this Act carries a duty to report`
           IF `Article 16: a case of the kind the national government analyzes` i
           THEN `no provision of this Act requires me to report it; the national government is to analyze cases like this one (Article 16)`
           OTHERWISE `no provision of this Act requires me to report it`

DECLARE `Penalty answer` IS ONE OF
    `this Act contains no penalty, fine or other sanction`
    `a provision of this Act carries a penalty, fine or other sanction`

@ref Articles 1 to 28 and Supplementary Provisions Articles 1 to 4, searched for a penalty
GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF `A provision`
GIVETH A `Penalty answer`
`can the business be penalised, reading` ps MEANS
    IF   `some provision carries` `a penalty, fine or other sanction` ps
    THEN `a provision of this Act carries a penalty, fine or other sanction`
    ELSE `this Act contains no penalty, fine or other sanction`

DECLARE `Naming answer` IS ONE OF
    `no provision of this Act provides for publishing my name`
    `a provision of this Act provides for publishing a name`

-- 公表 ("make public") occurs once in the Act, Article 18(4), and what is made
-- public there is the Artificial Intelligence Basic Plan.
@ref Articles 1 to 28 and Supplementary Provisions Articles 1 to 4, searched for publication of a name; Article 18(4)
GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF `A provision`
GIVETH A `Naming answer`
`can the business be named, reading` ps MEANS
    IF   `some provision carries` `publication of a person's name` ps
    THEN `a provision of this Act provides for publishing a name`
    ELSE `no provision of this Act provides for publishing my name`

DECLARE `Orders answer` IS ONE OF
    `no provision of this Act lets the government investigate or inspect me, order me, or require me to comply with a request`
    `a provision of this Act carries an investigation, inspection or order power, or a duty to comply`

@ref Articles 1 to 28 and Supplementary Provisions Articles 1 to 4, searched for investigation, inspection, orders and a duty to comply
GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF `A provision`
GIVETH AN `Orders answer`
`can the business be investigated or ordered, reading` ps MEANS
    IF      `some provision carries` `an investigation, inspection or order addressed to a private person` ps
         OR `some provision carries` `a duty to comply with a request` ps
    THEN `a provision of this Act carries an investigation, inspection or order power, or a duty to comply`
    ELSE `no provision of this Act lets the government investigate or inspect me, order me, or require me to comply with a request`
